NUM-12: include the volume below the first point of a storage curve

Below the first point of a storage curve SWMM takes the surface area to
grow linearly from 0 at depth 0, so the volume there is a1*x1/2.
table_getStorageVolume() used that triangle for depths up to x1 but
restarted from 0 above x1, while the inverse (depth from volume) included
it. A storage unit lost a1*x1/2 of volume the moment it filled past the
first point, which shows up as a routing continuity error. Start the
end-area sum from a1*x1/2. Curves whose first depth is 0 are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-12_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/table.c b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
index c7564d2..ce0fff3 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/table.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
@@ -614,6 +614,10 @@ double table_getStorageVolume(TTable *table, double x)
         return (a1/x1) * x * x / 2.0;
     }
 
+    // --- start from the volume below the first tabulated depth
+    //     (as in table_getStorageDepth)
+    v = a1 * x1 / 2.0;
+
     // --- otherwise traverse table entries until target depth is bracketed
     while (entry->next)
     {
